## DB-Backed “What We Did” Logging (App Development)
For ongoing app development, capture progress in the DB-backed memory tables:
- `task`/`run` for the unit of work
- `run_event` for append-only evidence (commands/errors/links)
- `library_item` for reusable knowledge; update by superseding (never delete)

Script (this repo):
- `scripts/log_tasks_library_frontend_progress.py`
  - Default: dry-run (read-only)
  - Write mode: pass `--apply`

## Demo Narrative (Customer Data Cleanup)
User is an engineer/technician doing recurring customer data cleanup.
- Run 1: user explains everything -> memory is Created/Promoted.
- Run 2: support ticket arrives with UUID1/UUID2/UUID3 -> system Utilizes memory; links show exactly what was reused.

## Guardrails
- Never store secrets in repo docs (DB URLs, tokens, passwords); use env vars.
- Do not delete memory entries; supersede instead to preserve trust.
- Keep run_event append-only; corrections should supersede prior event, not rewrite history.

